data: {"type":"response.output_item.done","sequence_number":909,"output_index":2,"item":{"type":"function_call","id":"fc_0f4e7e280b13e58d016acd1daecdd88195a10c4475b20ea0f4","call_id":"call_11a6b46f44f34bb6b4c3cb44a2b692b6","name":"edit","arguments":"{\"path\":\"server.js\",\"edits\":[{\"oldText\":\"// Existing tasks receive the same default as new tasks.\",\"newText\":\"// Existing projects start with Normal without changing their existing tasks.\\nif (!db.prepare('PRAGMA table_info(projects)').all().some((column) => column.name === 'default_priority')) {\\n  db.exec(\\\"ALTER TABLE projects ADD COLUMN default_priority TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'Normal' CHECK (default_priority IN ('Low', 'Normal', 'High'))\\\");\\n}\\n// Existing tasks retain their original Normal priority on migration.\"},{\"oldText\":\"const getProject = db.prepare('SELECT id, name, archived FROM projects WHERE id = ?');\",\"newText\":\"const getProject = db.prepare('SELECT id, name, archived, default_priority FROM projects WHERE id = ?');\\nconst setDefaultPriority = db.prepare('UPDATE projects SET default_priority = ? WHERE id = ?');\"},{\"oldText\":\"const createTask = db.prepare('INSERT INTO tasks (project_id, title) VALUES (?, ?)');\",\"newText\":\"const createTask = db.prepare('INSERT INTO tasks (project_id, title, priority) VALUES (?, ?, ?)');\"},{\"oldText\":\"    <form class=\\\"create task-create\\\" method=\\\"post\\\" action=\\\"/projects/${project.id}/tasks\\\">\",\"newText\":\"    <form class=\\\"filter\\\" method=\\\"post\\\" action=\\\"/projects/${project.id}/default-priority\\\">\\n      ${filterFields}\\n      <label for=\\\"default-task-priority\\\">Default task priority</label>\\n      <select id=\\\"default-task-priority\\\" name=\\\"priority\\\"${project.archived ? ' disabled' : ''} onchange=\\\"this.form.requestSubmit()\\\">\\n        ${priorities.map((option) => `<option${project.default_priority === option ? ' selected' : ''}>${option}</option>`).join('')}\\n      </select>\\n    </form>\\n    <form class=\\\"create task-create\\\" method=\\\"post\\\" action=\\\"/projects/${project.id}/tasks\\\">\"},{\"oldText\":\"    } else if (request.method === 'POST' && /^\\\\/projects\\\\/[1-9]\\\\d*\\\\/rename$/.test(url.pathname)) {\",\"newText\":\"    } else if (request.method === 'POST' && /^\\\\/projects\\\\/[1-9]\\\\d*\\\\/default-priority$/.test(url.pathname)) {\\n      const project = getProject.get(url.pathname.split('/')[2]);\\n      if (!project) {\\n        html(response, 404, page('Not found', '<h1>Project not found</h1>'));\\n        return;\\n      }\\n      const form = await readForm(request);\\n      const filter = taskFilter(form.get('filter'));\\n      const priority = priorityFilter(form.get('priorityFilter'));\\n      if (project.archived) {\\n        html(response, 403, projectPage(project, filter, 'Archived projects cannot be changed', priority));\\n        return;\\n      }\\n      const defaultPriority = form.get('priority');\\n      if (!priorities.includes(defaultPriority)) {\\n        html(response, 400, projectPage(project, filter, 'Invalid task priority', priority));\\n        return;\\n      }\\n      setDefaultPriority.run(defaultPriority, project.id);\\n      response.writeHead(303, { Location: projectLocation(project.id, filter, priority) });\\n      response.end();\\n    } else if (request.method === 'POST' && /^\\\\/projects\\\\/[1-9]\\\\d*\\\\/rename$/.test(url.pathname)) {\"},{\"oldText\":\"createTask.run(projectId, title);\",\"newText\":\"createTask.run(projectId, title, project.default_priority);\"}]}","status":"completed"}}

event: response.completed
data: {"type":"response.completed","sequence_number":910,"safety_buffering":false,"response":{"id":"resp_0f4e7e280b13e58d016acd1dac1eb08195b836ff1916dcb759","object":"response","created_at":1791827372,"completed_at":1791827386,"status":"completed","background":false,"frequency_penalty":0.0,"presence_penalty":0.0,"moderation":null,"model":"gpt-6.1-sol","access_programs":{"cyber":"standard"},"previous_response_id":null,"instructions":"You are an expert coding assistant operating inside pi, a coding agent harness. You help users by reading files, executing commands, editing code, and writing new files.\n\n<tools>\n- read: Read file contents\n- bash: Execute bash commands (ls, grep, find, etc.)\n- edit: Make precise file edits with exact text replacement, including multiple disjoint edits in one call\n- write: Create or overwrite files\n\nIn addition to the tools above, you may have access to other custom tools depending on the project.\n</tools>\n\n<rules>\n- Use bash for file operations like ls, rg, find\n- Use read to examine files instead of cat or sed.\n- You can inspect PI_* environment variables for current model and session details.\n- Use edit for precise changes (edits[].oldText must match exactly)\n- When changing multiple separate locations in one file, use one edit call with multiple entries in edits[] instead of multiple edit calls\n- Each edits[].oldText is matched against the original file, not after earlier edits are applied. Do not emit overlapping or nested edits. Merge nearby changes into one edit.\n- Keep edits[].oldText as small as possible while still being unique in the file. Do not pad with large unchanged regions.\n- Use write only for new files or complete rewrites.\n- Be concise in your responses\n- Show file paths clearly when working with files\n</rules>\n\n<docs>\nPi documentation (read only when the user asks about pi itself, its SDK, extensions, themes, skills, or TUI):\n- Main documentation: /usr/local/share/npm-global/lib/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/README.md\n- Additional docs: /usr/local/share/npm-global/lib/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/docs\n- Examples: /usr/local/share/npm-global/lib/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/examples (extensions, custom tools, SDK)\n- When reading pi docs or examples, resolve docs/... under Additional docs and examples/... under Examples, not the current working directory\n- When asked about: extensions (docs/extensions.md, examples/extensions/), themes (docs/themes.md), skills (docs/skills.md), prompt templates (docs/prompt-templates.md), TUI components (docs/tui.md), keybindings (docs/keybindings.md), SDK integrations (docs/sdk.md), custom providers (docs/custom-provider.md), adding models (docs/models.md), pi packages (docs/packages.md), environment variables (docs/environment-variables.md), MCP servers (docs/mcp.md), codemode scripts and non-LLM models such as classifiers and image models (docs/codemode.md)\n- When working on pi topics, read the docs and examples, and follow .md cross-references before implementing\n- Always read pi .md files completely and follow links to related docs (e.g., tui.md for TUI API details)\n</docs>\n\n<addendum>\nKeep changes focused and readable. Use clear names and avoid needless duplication. Verify the changed behavior with appropriate checks before submitting.\n</addendum>\n\n<cwd>\n/home/agent/work\n</cwd>","output":[{"type":"reasoning","id":"rs_0f4e7e280b13e58d016acd1dad4910819584d095ccb9a2e2a0","summary":[{"type":"summary_text","text":"**Implementing a targeted route**\n\nI’m thinking about how to implement a more concise and targeted route. I want to ensure it’s efficient and clear. What aspects should I focus on? Maybe I should think about the user’s needs and goals when determining the best path. Is there a way to gather feedback on how effective this route is? I wonder if mapping tools could provide some insights to help improve the approach too. Let's explore this further!"}],"